IMPORT prelude

-- Codex Insurance Limited -- Personal Accident and Sickness Policy
--
-- All dates/times below, apart from the claimant's age, are encoded as a
-- NUMBER of months elapsed since the policy's effective date. Every one of
-- the nine benchmark queries states its facts relative to the effective
-- date, so no DATE type, no calendar arithmetic, and no "elapsed time
-- between two dates" calculation is ever needed here -- every comparison is
-- a direct NUMBER comparison against a threshold drawn from the text (6, 7,
-- or 12 months).
--
-- This file defines ONLY the rules that decide whether a claim is covered.
-- No claim's data is defined here -- see apply.l4 for the nine queries.

§ `Codex Insurance Limited -- Personal Accident and Sickness Policy`

§§ `The facts of a single hospitalization claim`

DECLARE Claim HAS
    -- the claimant's age in whole years at the time of the hospitalization --
    -- the one fact that is NOT relative to the effective date
    `age at hospitalization`                                IS A NUMBER

    -- when the hospitalization occurred, in months after the effective date
    `hospitalization month`                                 IS A NUMBER

    -- §1.1.1: a benefit is only payable for a hospitalization "for sickness
    -- or accidental injury"
    `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury`  IS A BOOLEAN

    -- §2.1: the four activity-based exclusions. Each asks whether the event
    -- causing the sickness or injury arose directly or indirectly out of the
    -- named activity -- not merely whether the claimant happens to hold that
    -- occupation at the time.
    `event arose out of skydiving`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `event arose out of service in the military`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `event arose out of service as a fire fighter`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `event arose out of service in the police`              IS A BOOLEAN

    -- §1.3: no later than the 7th month anniversary, written confirmation of
    -- a wellness visit must be supplied to the Company. NOTHING means no
    -- confirmation has been supplied (yet).
    `wellness visit confirmation month`                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER

    -- §1.3: the wellness visit the confirmation attests to must itself have
    -- occurred no later than the 6th month anniversary. None of the nine
    -- benchmark queries give this sub-event its own relative month, so it is
    -- captured as a plain flag rather than as a second relative-month
    -- number.
    `wellness visit occurred no later than the 6th month`   IS A BOOLEAN

    -- §1.2 cancelation grounds unrelated to §1.3
    `claimant committed fraud`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `claimant made a misrepresentation`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `claimant materially withheld information`              IS A BOOLEAN

    -- §3.2: arbitration is a condition precedent to Our liability, but only
    -- where a dispute or disagreement exists in the first place.
    `dispute exists between the parties`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `valid arbitration award has been issued`               IS A BOOLEAN


§§ `1.1 - 1.3  Policy in effect and conditions`

-- §1.3, read together with §1.2: the wellness-visit condition is treated as
-- met -- for purposes of the policy remaining in effect -- whenever it has
-- either been satisfied on time or has not yet fallen due. Reading §1.2's
-- "has not been satisfied in a timely fashion" as anything broader than the
-- negation of that same disjunction would mean the 7-month grace period
-- promised by §1.3 could never actually be relied on: a claimant would
-- already be in breach on day one, before the deadline even arrives, merely
-- because confirmation has not yet been supplied. That reading would make
-- the grace period self-defeating, so §1.1(3) and §1.2 are encoded here as
-- two statements of one underlying condition, and this predicate is that
-- condition.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`condition 1.3 is satisfied or still pending` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `wellness visit confirmation month`
    WHEN JUST m THEN m AT MOST 7 AND claim's `wellness visit occurred no later than the 6th month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN claim's `hospitalization month` AT MOST 7

-- §3.6: the policy term is one year (12 months) from the effective date, and
-- §1.2 automatically cancels the policy on the last day of that term.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy term has expired` claim MEANS
    claim's `hospitalization month` GREATER THAN 12

-- §1.2: the grounds for automatic cancelation.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy has been canceled` claim MEANS
        claim's `claimant committed fraud`
    OR  claim's `claimant made a misrepresentation`
    OR  claim's `claimant materially withheld information`
    OR  NOT (`condition 1.3 is satisfied or still pending` claim)
    OR  `policy term has expired` claim

-- §1.1: the policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization if the
-- agreement is signed and the premium has been paid (assumed throughout,
-- per the task instructions -- no rule is needed for either), the §1.3
-- condition is pending-or-satisfied, and the policy has not been canceled.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization` claim MEANS
        `condition 1.3 is satisfied or still pending` claim
    AND NOT (`policy has been canceled` claim)


§§ `2.1  General exclusions`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a general exclusion applies` claim MEANS
        claim's `event arose out of skydiving`
    OR  claim's `event arose out of service in the military`
    OR  claim's `event arose out of service as a fire fighter`
    OR  claim's `event arose out of service in the police`
    OR  claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80


§§ `3.1  Territorial scope`

-- §3.1.1: the policy insures the claimant twenty-four hours a day, anywhere
-- in the world. This is an unconditional grant, not a restriction, so there
-- is no location-based fact to test and no predicate is needed for it.


§§ `3.2  Arbitration as a condition precedent to Our liability`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the arbitration precondition to liability is satisfied` claim MEANS
        NOT (claim's `dispute exists between the parties`)
    OR  claim's `valid arbitration award has been issued`


§§ `3.3 - 3.5  Governing law, currency, and premium`

-- §3.3 (New York law), §3.4 (payments in US currency), and §3.5 (the
-- premium is paid in one lump sum at signing) are procedural/boilerplate
-- terms. None of them condition whether a given hospitalization is covered,
-- so they add no predicate to the coverage decision below.


§§ `Coverage determination`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`covered` claim MEANS
        claim's `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury`
    AND `policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization` claim
    AND NOT (`a general exclusion applies` claim)
    AND `the arbitration precondition to liability is satisfied` claim
